haker (Mitsubishi Electric Research Laboratories)","venue":"US Patent Application US20240427327A1"},{"i":13,"f":"cloud","fields":["cloud","ai-systems"],"type":"system","year":2025,"name":"Secure, privacy-preserving LLM workflows","x":313.6,"y":255.4,"lay":4,"glyph":"square","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"project","href":"/projects/secure-llm-workflows/","summary":"Privacy-safe assistants and guardrails that let teams use LLMs over sensitive internal material without data leaving the trust boundary.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":20,"f":"cloud","fields":["cloud","ai-systems"],"type":"post","year":2026,"name":"The Branch Is the Variant: Zero-Copy, Privacy-Safe Test Data on a Versioned Lake","x":300.6,"y":262.8,"lay":4,"glyph":"triangle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"post","href":"/blogs/zero-copy-privacy-safe-test-data/","summary":"How a versioned data lake made the branch itself the test-data variant — zero-copy generation, blobstore-native metadata, and in-database hooks as the output channel.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":16,"f":"optimization","fields":["optimization","hyperspectral"],"type":"post","year":2026,"name":"Generate the Spectrum, Don't Store It: Physics as a Trainable Prior for Unmixing","x":449.9,"y":344.0,"lay":4,"glyph":"triangle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"post","href":"/blogs/differentiable-physics-for-hyperspectral-unmixing/","summary":"Why a 100-year-old optical-physics model, made differentiable, beats data-hungry neural nets at hyperspectral unmixing exactly when labeled data is scarce.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":18,"f":"bandits","fields":["bandits","robotics"],"type":"post","year":2026,"name":"One Coin Flip That Spans Fast Search and Cheap Search","x":594.7,"y":144.6,"lay":4,"glyph":"triangle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"post","href":"/blogs/multi-agent-search-with-bandits/","summary":"Two robotic-search strategies optimize opposite costs; randomly interleaving them with one tunable coin lets you slide between \"find targets now\" and \"spend the least energy.\"","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":1,"f":"bandits","fields":["bandits"],"type":"paper","year":2017,"name":"When to arrive in a congested system: Achieving equilibrium via learning algorithm","x":509,"y":99.4,"lay":5,"glyph":"circle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"paper","href":"/papers/when-to-arrive-congested-system-equilibrium-learning/","summary":"A distributed learning algorithm that lets players competing for an intermittently-available server choose when to sample it, converging to a unique Nash equilibrium while keeping sensing costs low.","authors":"P. Thaker, A. Gopalan, R. Vaze","venue":"ISIT 2017"},{"i":6,"f":"bandits","fields":["bandits"],"type":"paper","year":2022,"name":"Maximizing and Satisficing in Multi-armed Bandits with Graph Information","x":524,"y":99.4,"lay":5,"glyph":"circle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"paper","href":"/papers/maximizing-satisficing-bandits-graph/","summary":"A pure-exploration bandit method (GRUB and ζ-GRUB) that uses a similarity graph over arms to find the best arm, or one above a threshold, with far fewer samples than standard UCB.","authors":"P Thaker, M Malu, N Rao, G Dasarathy","venue":"NeurIPS 2022"},{"i":10,"f":"bandits","fields":["bandits"],"type":"paper","year":2024,"name":"Non-Stationary Bandits with Periodic Behavior via Ramanujan Periodicity Transforms","x":509,"y":90.4,"lay":5,"glyph":"circle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"paper","href":"/papers/non-stationary-bandits-periodic-behavior-ramanujan-transforms/","summary":"A multi-armed bandit method that uses the Ramanujan periodicity transform to detect periodic patterns in shifting rewards and exploit them to reduce regret.","authors":"P. Thaker, V. Gattani, V. Tirukkonda, P. Saidi, G. Dasarathy","venue":"ICASSP 2024"},{"i":2,"f":"optimization","fields":["optimization"],"type":"post","year":2018,"name":"Projected Gradient Descent with Skipping","x":518,"y":305.6,"lay":4,"glyph":"triangle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"post","href":"/blogs/projected-gradient-descent-skipping/","summary":"Exploring an interesting optimization technique that skips projection steps to potentially improve convergence in constrained convex optimization.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":22,"f":"optimization","fields":["optimization"],"type":"post","year":2026,"name":"Why You Can Start Gradient Descent Anywhere — Even on an NP-Hard Recovery Problem","x":533,"y":305.6,"lay":4,"glyph":"triangle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"post","href":"/blogs/nonconvex-landscape-of-quadratic-feasibility/","summary":"With order-n complex Gaussian quadratic measurements, recovering a vector up to phase becomes both identifiable and solvable by gradient descent from any starting point — two faces of one geometric condition.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":4,"f":"optimization","fields":["optimization"],"type":"paper","year":2020,"name":"On the Sample Complexity and Optimization Landscape for Quadratic Feasibility Problems","x":525.5,"y":278,"lay":5,"glyph":"circle","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"paper","href":"/papers/sample-complexity-optimization-landscape-quadratic-feasibility/","summary":"Proves identifiability and sample-complexity bounds for recovering a complex vector from quadratic measurements, and shows the nonconvex landscape lets gradient descent converge globally from arbitrary initialization.","authors":"P. K. Thaker, G. Dasarathy, A. Nedic","venue":"ISIT 2020"},{"i":5,"f":"bandits","fields":["bandits"],"type":"system","year":2022,"name":"GRUB: graph-informed pure-exploration bandits","x":492,"y":128.9,"lay":4,"glyph":"square","public":true,"evidence":true,"label":"project","href":"/projects/grub-graph-bandits/","summary":"Open-source bandit algorithms that use a similarity graph over arms to find the best (or good-enough) option with far fewer samples than standard UCB.","authors":null,"venue":null},{"i":15,"f":"bandits",